PocketPal design language (normative summary). Full spec with rationale + examples: `frontend/DESIGN_LANGUAGE.md`. Keep both in sync.

Principles:
- Clarity over decoration; one clear hero metric per screen, supporting detail muted.
- Trust through consistency: same action looks/behaves the same everywhere.
- Accessibility (WCAG AA, keyboard, focus-visible, prefers-reduced-motion) is a foundation, not a QA step.
- Motion is functional: every animation does one job (feedback, attention, state, spatial) or is removed.

Color:
- Use semantic tokens only (`primary`, `muted`, `destructive`, `card`, `glass-*`, `chart-1..5`, `sidebar-*`). Never raw hex/oklch in components.
- Color by intent, not by habit: income/positive, expense, savings, status each map to an intent token. Do NOT make every metric/icon green.
- Red is reserved for errors + destructive actions.
- Dark mode is first-class (`dark:` variants). Verify contrast, especially text on glass.

Typography:
- Font `font-sans` (DM Sans). 1.25 scale; weights 400/500/600.
- Mandatory `tabular-nums` on ALL money, percentages, and counts (KPIs, table cells, chart axes).

Spacing & layout:
- 4px grid / 8px rhythm: `gap-2/4/6/8`, `p-4/6/8`. No arbitrary one-off values.
- Use `app-content-frame`, `app-page-grid` + `GridItem`, `app-page-stack`. Radius scale from `--radius` (`rounded-lg/md/sm`, pills `rounded-full`).

Surfaces (glass vs flat) — decide by density, not by screen:
- Glass (`.glass`/`.app-surface`/`glass-strong`): shell, header, nav, KPI cards, modals/sheets/popovers, auth hero.
- Liquid Glass (`.liquid-glass`/`.liquid-glass-strong`, `--lg-*` tokens): preferred material for those same chrome/KPI/modal surfaces. Tier 2 `.liquid-glass-refract` is progressive-only (Chromium; falls back to Tier 1) and must keep the opaque `--lg-fallback` for `prefers-reduced-transparency`/`prefers-contrast`. Never behind dense data.
- Opaque `card`: dense/text-heavy surfaces — tables, forms, settings panels.
- Never put `backdrop-blur` on tiny elements (e.g. icon tiles). Shadows only from `--shadow-*`/`shadow-glass`/`shadow-liquid`.

Icons:
- `lucide-react` only. `size-4` inline, `size-5` standalone. Decorative → `aria-hidden`; icon-only controls → `aria-label` (+ tooltip when meaning isn't obvious, e.g. collapsed sidebar).

Motion (tokens to adopt; ranges enforced now):
- Durations: micro 100-200ms (`--motion-fast` 120), component 200-300ms (`--motion-standard` 220), page 300-500ms (`--motion-slow` 400). Never > 500ms.
- Easing: enter = ease-out (`--ease-enter`), exit = ease-in (`--ease-exit`, faster than enter), A→B = ease-in-out (`--ease-standard`). `linear` only for indeterminate spinners.
- Animate `transform`/`opacity` only (no width/height/top/left/box-shadow). Initial-viewport motion ≤ 800ms total; scroll reveals fire once.
- Always honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Implement with CSS + `tw-animate-css` + Radix `data-[state]`. No new animation library without approval (`.cursor/rules/dependencies-approval.mdc`).

Components (prefer shadcn/ui + Radix; compose, don't fork):
- Define states: default/hover/active/focus-visible/disabled/loading/empty/error.
- Buttons: one primary per view; destructive uses `destructive`; show spinner + disabled while pending.
- Forms: every input has a Label or aria-label; use shadcn `Checkbox`/`Switch` (no raw `<input type=checkbox>`).
- Tables: money columns right-aligned + `tabular-nums`; provide loading/empty/error states; mobile = card list.
- Modals/sheets: Radix wrappers with title + description and focus management.
- Nav: consistent active treatment across sidebar + bottom nav.

Data display & states:
- Currency via `Intl.NumberFormat`, locale derived from currency/user (not hardcoded en-IN). Mask sensitive numbers (`•••• 1234`).
- Empty states = onboarding (icon + guidance + primary CTA); distinguish "no data yet" from "no results for filters" (offer Clear filters). Use skeletons matching final layout; spinners only for in-button async.
- One shared error treatment with retry.

Never:
- Ship mocked/hardcoded data, dead actions, fake profile defaults, or permanent placeholder columns/fields ("—").
- Mix premium auth + plain app surfaces.
- Left-align proportional-digit money, drop in raw HTML form controls, or use inline ad-hoc/linear UI timings.
